msgid "Art. L.124-5 & L.124-11 · Code du travail"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dismissal & Termination Disputes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dismissed with notice (licenciement avec préavis) or for serious misconduct "
"(faute grave)? In Luxembourg, you have 1 month to request the written "
"reasons by registered letter and 3 months to contest an abusive dismissal."
msgstr ""

msgid "Assess a dismissal issue"
msgstr ""

msgid "Art. L.246-1 to L.246-7 · Law of 29 March 2023"
msgstr ""

msgid "Moral Harassment (Mobbing) & Burnout"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Facing repeated hostility, isolation, or toxic management pressure? "
"Luxembourg law obliges employers to stop moral harassment, protects victims "
"and witnesses from retaliation, and empowers the Staff Delegation and ITM to"
" intervene."
msgstr ""

msgid "Assess a harassment issue"
msgstr ""

msgid "Art. L.211-27 & L.221-1 · Wages & Hours"
msgstr ""

msgid "Unpaid Overtime, Salary & Indexation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Missing wage indexation (tranche indiciaire), uncompensated overtime, "
"withheld bonuses, or refused statutory leave? Wage claims in Luxembourg "
"remain enforceable for 3 years with strong documentary evidence."
msgstr ""

msgid "Assess a salary or overtime issue"
msgstr ""

msgid "Art. L.121-6 · Incapacity & Maternity"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sick Leave & Protected Employees"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Notified your employer on day 1 and submitted your medical certificate by "
"day 3? You are legally shielded from dismissal for up to 26 weeks of sick "
"leave, as well as during pregnancy, parental leave, or staff delegate "
"mandates."
msgstr ""

msgid "Assess sick leave protection"
msgstr ""

msgid "Art. L.121-7 · Contract Clauses"
msgstr ""

msgid "Unilateral Contract Modification"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Pressured to sign an addendum (avenant) reducing your pay, changing your "
"workplace, or stripping responsibilities? Unfavorable changes to essential "
"contract terms must follow strict notice and pre-interview rules."
msgstr ""

